WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:25.199 --> 00:00:27.199
I want to show you two sequences that if

00:00:27.199 --> 00:00:28.640
you're only given a few terms

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:31.920
they are really hard. They both appeared

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.960
in Eureka, in this magazine, in their

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:36.320
puzzle section.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:38.399
The first one I can do without

00:00:38.399 --> 00:00:40.559
cheating and it goes like this:

00:00:40.559 --> 00:00:45.271
3, 4, 6, 8,

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:52.160
nine, ten - no - eleven, no, twelve?

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:55.280
Yeah 12. Thirteen?

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:58.800
Fourteen - I've already given
you more than

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:01.760
the Eureka puzzle gave you. So what's the

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:02.480
formula?

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:05.119
There's a very simple formula but you

00:01:05.119 --> 00:01:06.909
really won't guess it.

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:10.640
It's really annoying, you can see

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:12.400
why I hate these puzzles,

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.479
if they only give you a few terms. Let's

00:01:14.479 --> 00:01:16.000
subtract 1 and we get

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.200
2, 3, 5, 7,

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:23.040
11, 13 - the primes.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.840
So this sequence: it goes up by one, then

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:28.080
it goes up by two, and two, and four

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:30.079
oh and then two and so on - it looks like

00:01:30.079 --> 00:01:32.479
it's something to do with adding twos

00:01:32.479 --> 00:01:35.520
but in fact subtract one and it becomes

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:39.280
transparent. This is the kind of thing

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:41.920
where even if you say 'yes, all right,

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:42.640
there are mil-

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:44.960
but there are a million ways to extend

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:47.040
the sequence to explain the sequence'

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.920
but when you see the the answer, the the-

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:51.119
this is a good puzzle

00:01:51.119 --> 00:01:53.759
in the sense that it's puzzling and yet

00:01:53.759 --> 00:01:55.280
when you see the answer

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:57.600
you say all right yes I admit

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:59.680
that's what the answer has to be.

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:02.241
(Brady: So these were the
the primes plus 1 basically?)

00:02:02.241 --> 00:02:03.520
Yes that's all.

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:05.360
(Okay, I'm going to come up with my own)

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:06.880
(sequence and just make it the primes)

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:08.160
(plus 8 or something and-)

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:10.479
Yeah you could certainly, just as hard -

00:02:10.479 --> 00:02:12.080
harder, because it probably isn't in the

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:13.360
OEIS.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:15.120
There's a related one and now I can do

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:17.599
it without cheating, it goes like this:

00:02:17.599 --> 00:02:19.791
5, 8,

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:24.184
12 ,18, 24.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:26.959
Now you look at that and you say, well

00:02:26.959 --> 00:02:29.520
look, we've got 6 times 2, 6 times 3,

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:30.959
6 times 4,

00:02:30.959 --> 00:02:32.080
and then there are a couple of

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:34.160
experimental errors at the beginning.

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:36.160
Basically this is going to be multiples

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:37.680
of six right?

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:41.080
Wrong! You want a chance
to think about it?

00:02:47.519 --> 00:02:50.560
(All right, back in the room)
- Back in the room

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:52.640
here's the answer. Let me change these

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:54.160
commas to pluses:

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:57.200
2 plus 3, 3 plus 5,

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.920
5 plus 7, 7 plus 11 - it's

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:01.120
the sums

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:04.400
of two consecutive primes. Isn't that

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:05.200
annoying?

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:08.319
And yet when you see it it's clearly the

00:03:08.319 --> 00:03:09.519
right answer.

00:03:09.519 --> 00:03:12.239
So when you're given one of these

00:03:12.239 --> 00:03:13.680
puzzles

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:16.000
on a quiz or an IQ test or a job

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.280
interview or something

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:19.519
the first thing you should do is excuse

00:03:19.519 --> 00:03:20.319
yourself.

00:03:20.319 --> 00:03:22.720
Go to the bathroom and look it up in the

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:24.180
OEIS.

